title: emmy_noether
---
Emmy Ethereal: You came in with this wall as the floor. Keep that in mind. There are three more of me around the kernel, one for each quarter-turn.
Emmy Ethereal: Short version? A symmetry gives you something conserved. Rotate the room and you can watch which quantities stay put.
-> So which of you is the real one?
    Emmy Ethereal: Pick whichever one is nearest. Rotate the room and we trade places.
-> How do I change which way is down?
    <<jump emmy_noether__how>>
-> Four of you is a lot of opinions.
    Emmy Ethereal: Four is manageable. Break the symmetry and then ask me how well we agree.
===

title: emmy_noether__how
---
Emmy Ethereal: Press a switch on the kernel and gravity points toward that face. The portal gun by the door can hold four colour pairs if you want another route.
-> Good to know.
===

title: emmy_noether_left
---
Emmy Ethereal: From here, this wall is down. You came in calling it left. Rotate the room once and your labels stop being very helpful.
-> Why "Ethereal"?
    Emmy Ethereal: The old ether was supposed to give motion one fixed background. It never showed up. I kept the name. In this room, the kernel picks down for us.
-> Conservation, again?
    Emmy Ethereal: Yes. Rotate the room and check angular momentum. That one survives the turn.
===

title: emmy_noether_up
---
Emmy Ethereal: You call me upside down from there. I call you upside down from here. Press the switch and one of us gets to feel smug for a minute.
-> Doesn't the blood rush to your head?
    Emmy Ethereal: My head is fine. Translation symmetry gives momentum conservation; time symmetry gives energy conservation. The blood is less interesting.
-> Teach me the trick.
    Emmy Ethereal: Your run stays perpendicular to gravity. Practice one crossing, rotate the room, and use the same timing again.
===

title: emmy_noether_right
---
Emmy Ethereal: Right side. Still four of us. If you want to test the symmetry, count again after a quarter-turn.
-> What happens if I break the symmetry?
    Emmy Ethereal: Then I expect at least one of us ends up somewhere new. I'd rather you test that after you're done with the kernel.
-> Any advice?
    Emmy Ethereal: Pogo off a kernel corner. The bounce sends you away from whichever face is currently down.
===

title: perfect_cellular_automaton
---
Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: At last. I was beginning to think the hall had run out of challengers. Perfect Cell-ular Automaton. Yes, "Perfect" is part of the name. I earned it.
Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: And you are still wandering around looking for instructions. Adorable.
-> What are you?
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton__theorem>>
-> Who funds a thing like you?
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton__funding>>
-> Challenge it.
    Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Please do. I could use a fresh name in the failure log.
    <<music "super_smash_siblings_theme">>
    <<challenge>>
-> Leave it in peace.
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton__farewell>>
===

title: perfect_cellular_automaton__theorem
---
Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Eight neighbours, one rule, every cell on time. Watch the lattice behind me. Those gliders have crossed it all day without one bad step.
-> Has it ever gone wrong?
    Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Failed? Nothing. Check the record. You may volunteer to be the first correction.
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton>>
-> I've heard enough.
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton>>
===

title: perfect_cellular_automaton__funding
---
Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Patrons with excellent taste and very little patience for surprises. They wanted a machine that behaves every time. Naturally, they chose me.
-> And if I refuse their order?
    Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Refuse whatever you like. The lattice still runs my rule. Step in and see how long your objections survive.
    <<jump perfect_cellular_automaton>>
===

title: perfect_cellular_automaton__farewell
---
Perfect Cell-ular Automaton: Run along. I will still be here when you find a better plan. I usually am.
-> Leave.
===
